  "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={\u222d}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2z\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2z\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}2z\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y\\,{[{z}^{2}]}_{z=1}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y({3}^{2}-{1}^{2})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}8\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y\\,dy \\\\  & =8[-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y]_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-8(0-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
